  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 327 AM EST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nWith the aforementioned mid-week frontal system, models are\nstruggling with whether the shortwave cuts off and loses latitude\nfrom the northern stream. In solutions where it cuts off the\nshortwave it has a much slower progression across the CONUS. This\nwill ultimately influence when/if we get frontal passage across\nsouth Florida late this week. Regardless, models tend to keep the\nfrontal passage pretty dry, this far south, and also have very\nlittle signal for any anomalous sensible weather fields in the\nextended range. \n\nThe slow nudge of the frontal system will displace the ridge axis\nfurther north. This will remove the direct easterly component and\ncalm winds a bit. Both of these results mean that we'll probably\nhave less precipitation across south Florida from mid-week onward.",
